The [b]realloc()[/b] function expands a current block to include additional memory.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="c" codeId="2124"]int *ptr;
ptr = malloc(10 * sizeof(*ptr));  
if (ptr != NULL) {
  *(ptr + 2) = 50;  /* assign 50 to third int */
}
ptr = [b]realloc(ptr, 100 * sizeof(*ptr))[/b]; 
*(ptr + 30) = 75; [/code]
[b]realloc[/b] leaves the original content in memory and expands the block to allow for more storage.
